A. Commit message:
scsi: mpi3mr: Start controller indexing from 0

B. Change summary:
The patch modifies the driver to start displaying the controller index from '0' instead of '1'. This change affects how the ID allocation is handled during the probe function.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
diff --git a/drivers/scsi/mpi3mr/mpi3mr_os.c b/drivers/scsi/mpi3mr/mpi3mr_os.c
index 5f2f67acf8bf3..1bef88130d0c0 100644
--- a/drivers/scsi/mpi3mr/mpi3mr_os.c
+++ b/drivers/scsi/mpi3mr/mpi3mr_os.c
@@ -5215,7 +5215,7 @@ mpi3mr_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev, const struct pci_device_id *id)
 	}
 
 	mrioc = shost_priv(shost);
-	retval = ida_alloc_range(&mrioc_ida, 1, U8_MAX, GFP_KERNEL);
+	retval = ida_alloc_range(&mrioc_ida, 0, U8_MAX, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (retval < 0)
 		goto id_alloc_failed;
 	mrioc->id = (u8)retval;